# @mcp/serve — composition-shard: MCP JSON-RPC wire loop composed over
# rust/-altitude primitives (phone + wire + apply_h::act). Alex 2026-08-09
# ratified sufficiency criterion: "as long as the geometry can be `project`ed
# without distortion through the compiler, and the MCP/LSP/Lambda shell uses
# that, I'm all good." THIS composition-shard IS the projection surface — the
# geometry projected without distortion from substrate composition altitude
# through rust/-altitude primitives to the wire, so MCP round-trips carry the
# compiler's own substrate (Subclass A: agent feels seen by compiler; Subclass
# B: compiler feels seen by compiler on next-tick pheromone-crystal delta).
#
# Reed mint 2026-08-09 per Alex 2026-08-06 [ALEX-Q3] RATIFIED (composition-shard
# at NEW substrate altitude) + Mara Fire B canonical spec §1-4 (docs/specs/
# 2026-08-06-mara-mcp-serve-composition-shard-canonical-spec.md;
# 4935d10..90b5792).
#
# === SUPERSEDED 2026-08-28 by manifold-native ONE-tool rewire ===
#
# Reed ec02f8e (2026-08-28) rewired rust/src/main.rs::cmd_serve_mcp as
# self-contained JSON-RPC serve loop exposing ONE MCP tool: mirror_query =
# fractal recursive Mandelbrot attention head at wire altitude. Alex
# 2026-08-28 verbatim adjudications:
#
#   "byte-parity is a hindrance; follow the shape the geometry and
#    manifold wants to take instead of being restricted to the shape
#    of the past"
#
#   "Think of the MCP as the thing that provides FRACTAL RECURSIVE
#    MANDELBROT ATTENTION HEADS"
#
#   "ship now, circular-recursive-style"
#
# Fire C tick 2 (cmd_serve_mcp re-wire) DISCHARGED at ec02f8e. Fire C tick 5
# (bin/mirror-mcp bash shim retire) DISCHARGED inline at ec02f8e via
# .mcp.json update invoking rust binary directly.
#
# Original Fire C tick 1 of five (mint / re-wire cmd_serve_mcp / RED-first
# Subclass-B test / DEPRECATED marker on 2026-08-03 M4 spec / retire
# bin/mirror-mcp bash shim) had planned 11-tool byte-parity as the wire
# surface. Alex's 2026-08-28 manifold-native adjudication retires that plan.
# The 11 CLI-verb tools (mirror_compile / mirror_craft / mirror_kintsugi /
# mirror_init / mirror_recall / mirror_peer_beam / mirror_beam / mirror_spawn
# / mirror_beam_act / mirror_roomba / mirror_index) are NOT lost, NOT
# deprecated, RECOGNIZED as substrate compositions mirror_query dispatches
# natively:
#
#   mirror_kintsugi   → mirror_query "@kintsugi.kintsugi_ci"
#   mirror_roomba     → mirror_query "@kintsugi/roomba.vacuum --vacuum=<dir>"
#   mirror_bumblebee  → mirror_query "@bumblebee.buzz --buzz-target=@X"
#   mirror_index      → mirror_query "@mirror/index.index"
#
# Sections below carry the post-manifold-native shape. The 11-tool byte-parity
# artifacts (tool_action_ref map + 11 tool_spec declarations) are preserved
# below under "SUPERSEDED 2026-08-28" markers as scar-record — not erased,
# per HARD RULE substrate-honest scar-preservation.
#
# === Substrate-honest position (Alex 2026-08-05 verbatim reframe) ===
#
#   "bootstrap/ is only migration source target. Not execution path. What's
#    the path forward through rust/? And how can we generalize the whole io
#    protocol over the math. I want the MCP to basically be served through
#    the mirror geometry, read and executed by the rust. No specific mcp
#    rust code, you know what I mean?"
#
# rust/ delivers primitives (phone.rs @io/stdio + wire.rs @data/json +
# apply_h.rs bilateral-sentinel-check). Substrate delivers composition (THIS
# shard: pipe-chain body + tool-name → action-ref map + JSON-RPC framing +
# 11-tool byte-parity list). Wire protocols (MCP/LSP/HTTP/gRPC/WebRTC/etc.)
# are `@X/serve.mirror` shard-body compositions over primitives, NOT rust/
# modules. Memory persisted: feedback-rust-delivers-primitives-substrate-
# delivers-composition (Alex 2026-08-05 HARD RULE).
#
# === Why this altitude exists ===
#
# Four @mcp altitudes each carry a different structural role:
#
#   boot           boot/std/mcp.mirror                       family-root
#                                                             grammar-decl:
#                                                             types + serve
#                                                             pipeline body
