# === serve_well_formed — bilateral predicate (Subclass A Förster criterion) ===
#
# Does every well-formed JSON-RPC request drive a well-formed JSON-RPC response
# through the pipe chain? Per JSON-RPC 2.0 §4 (well-formed request: jsonrpc
# "2.0" + method string + params object|array + id string|integer|null) + §5
# (well-formed response: jsonrpc "2.0" + (result|error) + id). Malformed
# requests surface as JSON-RPC error envelopes per §5.1; NEVER as pipe-chain
# panics.
#
# Förster-Slap Property 1 (Sudden) at wire altitude: verdict returns in one
# apply_h::act tick; no gradient partial-verdicts at composition altitude.
#
# Rice-safe bound: reads only byte-visible state (JSON-RPC envelope schema
# validity + response completeness); no program semantics inspection.
#
# Sentinel: `serve=jsonrpc2-round-trip-well-formed` — byte-level substrate-
# decl'd marker the resolver checks. When request+response round-trip
# satisfies JSON-RPC 2.0 §4+§5 envelope validity, realization layer stamps
# the sentinel; discharge is byte-equality.
#
# `\`-obligation-blocked; Fire C tick 3 (RED-first empirical test) composes
# via apply_h::act sentinel-check.
bilateral serve_well_formed {
  sentinel "serve=jsonrpc2-round-trip-well-formed"
  arity 1
}
serve_well_formed(frame: jsonrpc_frame) -> verdict { \ }

# === dispatch_composes_via_act — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the @mcp.dispatch body dispatch via apply_h::act (rust/-altitude
# bilateral-predicate dispatch primitive) for tool-name → action-ref
# resolution + verdict marshaling — NEVER via hardcoded rust/-altitude match
# arm? Per Alex 2026-08-05 substrate-honest reframe: wire-protocol logic
# lives at substrate composition altitude; rust/ altitude carries primitives
# ONLY.
#
# Förster-Slap Property 2 (Uninvited) at wire altitude: coupling structurally
# open once MCP client connects; dispatch body responds through coupling
# already-there without client's explicit invitation per response.
#
# Rice-safe bound: reads only byte-visible state (composition-shard body
# text contains `apply_h.act` invocation in dispatch match arms).
#
# Sentinel: `dispatch=apply-h-act-composed` — substrate-decl'd marker. When
# THIS shard's dispatch body composes via apply_h.act (grep-verifiable at
# substrate composition altitude), realization layer stamps sentinel;
# discharge is byte-equality.
#
# `\`-obligation-blocked; Fire C tick 3 composes via apply_h::act sentinel-
# check.
bilateral dispatch_composes_via_act {
  sentinel "dispatch=apply-h-act-composed"
  arity 1
}
dispatch_composes_via_act(shard_body: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === tools_reflects_landed_shards — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the @mcp.tools body reflect landed shard corpus (Phase 2 M5)? Phase 1
# hardcoded 11-tool byte-parity discharges the empirical claim; Phase 2
# reflective walk discharges the structural claim.
#
# Förster-Slap Property 3 (Loving-in-structure) at wire altitude: tool
# response widens what client can do next — adding a substrate shard with
# @mcp/tool annotation ADDS a wire tool (never removes); aperture-widening =
# choice-count-increase per Foerster ethical imperative operationalized.
#
# Rice-safe bound Phase 1: reads only byte-visible state (11-tool JSON
# literal matches bootstrap/src/mcp.rs::tools_list_result byte-parity).
# Phase 2: reads only byte-visible state (@mcp/tool annotations on landed
# shard bilateral blocks).
#
# Sentinel POST-2026-08-28 manifold-native rewire:
# `tools=manifold-native-one-tool-mirror-query` — substrate-decl'd marker.
# The predicate discharges when @mcp.tools body-fill returns exactly one
# tool_spec (tool_mirror_query) per manifold-native ONE-tool geometry, AND
# the wire response's tools array contains exactly one entry with
# name="mirror_query". Aperture-widening happens at the MQ-expression
# dispatch altitude (adding a landed bilateral extends the set of
# dispatchable action_refs) NOT at the tools/list altitude.
#
# SUPERSEDED 2026-08-28 sentinels (preserved as scar-record):
#   `tools=11-tool-byte-parity`         (Phase 1; retired)
#   `tools=reflective-walk-annotations` (Phase 2 M5; retired —
#                                        annotations landscape moves INTO
#                                        apply_h::act dispatch, not
#                                        tools/list expansion)
#
# `\`-obligation-blocked; empirical fire at Reed ec02f8e (2026-08-28)
# via mcp__mirror__mirror_query round-trip verified 6/6 JSON-RPC smoke
# frames (initialize + notifications/initialized + tools/list + tools/call
# {valid+empty+unknown-tool} + unknown-method).
bilateral tools_reflects_landed_shards {
  sentinel "tools=manifold-native-one-tool-mirror-query"
  arity 1
}
tools_reflects_landed_shards(tools_body: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === serve_witnessing — composed bilateral (Förster-Slap Property 4) ===
#
# The composed predicate consumers cite in `requires` clauses. Passes iff
# serve_well_formed AND dispatch_composes_via_act AND tools_reflects_landed_
# shards all discharge Pass over one JSON-RPC round-trip through THIS
# composition-shard.
#
# Förster-Slap Property 4 (Irreversible) at wire altitude: on Pass, the
# round-trip deposits pheromone-crystal at @mirror/store (via the invoked
# tool's own substrate-mutation — e.g. mirror_roomba deposits at docs/
# bauchladen/); next-tick @mirror/store observes own delta = Subclass B
# self-slap; ouroboros closes.
#
# Consumer surface (Fire C tick 2 rust/-altitude cmd_serve_mcp re-wire):
#   require serve_witnessing(frame)
#
# Sentinel: `serve=three-property-forster-slap` — all four properties
# byte-visible.
#
# `\`-obligation-blocked; realization discharges per-round-trip when Fire C
# tick 3 empirical test fires.
bilateral serve_witnessing {
  sentinel "serve=three-property-forster-slap"
  arity 1
}
serve_witnessing(frame: jsonrpc_frame) -> verdict {
  serve_well_formed(frame)
    |> compose(dispatch_composes_via_act(shard_body_of(frame)))
    |> compose(tools_reflects_landed_shards(tools_body_of(frame)))
}

